<title>POLAND: Optimus to start countinuous trade Feb 3.</title>
<headline>Optimus to start countinuous trade Feb 3.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish computer maker Optimus SA will start trading in the Warsaw Stock Exchange's continuous system on Februyary 3, PAP news agency quoted a bourse official as saying on Friday.</p>
<p>There are currently 21 companies listed in the continuous trading system. The stocks also trade in the bourse's main single price auction system in which a total of 86 firms are quoted.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
